<section class="legal-section">

  <div class="legal-shell">

    <article class="legal-content">

      <p>
        This Cookie Policy explains how STI Asset Management ("STI Asset Management", "we", "us" or "our") uses cookies and similar technologies when you visit or interact with our website. This Cookie Policy should be read together with our <a href="/privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a>, which provides additional information about how we collect, use, store and protect personal information.
      </p>


      <h2>
        1. What Are Cookies?
      </h2>

      <p>
        Cookies are small pieces of data stored on a user's device when a website is visited.
      </p>

      <p>
        Cookies can help websites operate correctly, maintain secure sessions, remember certain preferences and understand how visitors interact with website features.
      </p>

      <p>
        Some cookies remain only for the duration of a browsing session, while others may remain on a device for a specified period unless deleted earlier.
      </p>


      <h2>
        2. How We Use Cookies
      </h2>

      <p>
        STI Asset Management may use cookies and similar technologies to:
      </p>

      <ul>
        <li>
          Operate essential website functionality.
        </li>

        <li>
          Maintain secure user sessions.
        </li>

        <li>
          Support authentication and client login functionality.
        </li>

        <li>
          Protect website forms and services against misuse or unauthorised activity.
        </li>

        <li>
          Remember certain website preferences where applicable.
        </li>

        <li>
          Support website performance and functionality where applicable.
        </li>
      </ul>


      <h2>
        3. Strictly Necessary Cookies
      </h2>

      <p>
        Strictly necessary cookies are required for the website to function correctly and securely.
      </p>

      <p>
        They may be used for purposes such as maintaining a user session, authenticating users, protecting forms, preserving security settings and preventing fraudulent or unauthorised activity.
      </p>

      <p>
        Because these cookies are necessary to provide requested website functionality, disabling them may cause certain areas of the website or client portal to stop working correctly.
      </p>


      <h2>
        4. Preference Cookies
      </h2>

      <p>
        Where enabled, preference cookies allow the website to remember choices made by a visitor, such as interface or website preferences, so that those choices do not have to be selected again during future visits.
      </p>

      <p>
        STI Asset Management will only use such cookies where the relevant functionality is implemented on the website.
      </p>


      <h2>
        5. Analytics Cookies
      </h2>

      <p>
        STI Asset Management does not currently use optional analytics cookies.
      </p>

      <p>
        If analytics technologies are introduced in the future, this Cookie Policy and our cookie controls will be updated accordingly.
      </p>


      <h2>
        6. Third-Party Cookies
      </h2>

      <p>
        Certain website functionality may involve services provided by third parties, such as embedded maps, videos or other external content.
      </p>

      <p>
        These third parties may place or access cookies when their services are loaded.
      </p>

      <p>
        STI Asset Management does not control cookies independently placed by third-party services. Users should review the applicable third party's privacy and cookie information for further details.
      </p>


      <h2>
        7. Managing Your Cookie Preferences
      </h2>

      <p>
        Where optional cookies are used, visitors may be provided with controls that allow them to accept, reject or manage available cookie categories.
      </p>

      <p>
        Cookies can also generally be managed or deleted through browser settings. Blocking certain cookies may affect the functionality or performance of parts of the website.
      </p>

      <p>
        Strictly necessary cookies required for the operation and security of the website may continue to operate where they are required to provide a service requested by the user.
      </p>


      <h2>
        8. Cookie Retention
      </h2>

      <p>
        The length of time a cookie remains on a device depends on the purpose and type of cookie.
      </p>

      <p>
        Session cookies normally expire when a browsing session ends, when a user signs out, or after an applicable session timeout.
      </p>

      <p>
        Where persistent cookies are used, they may remain for a defined period or until they are deleted through the user's browser or cookie-management settings.
      </p>


      <h2>
        9. Personal Data and Cookies
      </h2>

      <p>
        Where information collected through cookies constitutes personal data, that information will be processed in accordance with our <a href="/privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a> and applicable data protection requirements.
      </p>

      <p>
        STI Asset Management will take appropriate measures to protect personal information collected through website technologies.
      </p>


      <h2>
        10. Changes to This Cookie Policy
      </h2>

      <p>
        STI Asset Management may update this Cookie Policy from time to time to reflect changes in the cookies we use, website functionality, regulatory requirements or applicable law.
      </p>

      <p>
        Updated versions will be published on this page, and users are encouraged to review the Cookie Policy periodically.
      </p>


